[
    {
        "content": "<p>I want to express the following statement \"there exists a unique <code>x</code> which satisfies <code>p</code>, and moreover this <code>x</code> also satisfies <code>q</code>\" (but <code>q</code> does not affect the uniqueness). For the sake of readability I would like to state this without having to repeat <code>p</code> or <code>q</code>.</p>\n<p>This can be encoded e.g. as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ExistsUniqueAnd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Does something like this exist in Mathlib? I think the conventional <code>ExistsUnique</code> does not cover this use case.</p>",
        "id": 614598971,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1785866481
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>if the <code>x</code> is unique, can it be a <code>def</code> instead?</p>",
        "id": 614603572,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1785867805
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In principle, yes. But in my case the expression is already nested within a number of quantifiers, and I would rather not introduce extraneous <code>def</code>s.</p>\n<p>To illustrate, my complete statement looks something like 'given a bunch of assumptions, there exists a unique solution to a PDE, which moreover satisfies ...'</p>",
        "id": 614604607,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1785868195
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would expect that to be something like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution_unique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">assumptions</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSolution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution_also</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">assumptions</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MoreoverSatisfies</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 614606912,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785869034
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That also has the advantage that you can have different assumptions for uniqueness and the further properties</p>",
        "id": 614606959,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785869052
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Will mathlib accept <code>def</code>s named <code>theSolution</code> or similar, for such cases?<br>\n(when the definition is <code>Exists.choose ...</code>, and there's no better descriptive name)</p>",
        "id": 614607750,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1785869331
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would be quite surprised if the definition is <code>Exists.choose</code> if you subsequently prove uniqueness</p>",
        "id": 614608181,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785869493
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Real.pi#doc\">docs#Real.pi</a></p>",
        "id": 614608241,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1785869513
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thats <code>f (Exists.choose _)</code> not <code>Exists.choose</code> :)</p>",
        "id": 614608349,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785869549
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess I should mention that none of my code in this case is intended for mathlib. I am merely trying to formalize the statement of one of my own papers.</p>\n<p>But more generally, wouldn't it be nice to be able to efficiently say \"there exists a unique <code>x</code> satisfying <code>p</code>, which moreover satisfies <code>q</code>?\". In my experience this phrasing is quite common in informal maths.</p>",
        "id": 614608413,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1785869567
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My impression is that informal math you can often end up with</p>\n<ul>\n<li>there exists a unique <code>x</code> satisfying <code>p</code>, which moreover satisfies <code>q</code>?</li>\n<li>later: the solution <code>x</code> also satisfies <code>q2</code></li>\n<li>later still: the solution <code>x</code> also satisfies <code>q4</code></li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 614608579,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785869627
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Any backreference of this form is really saying that this was a definition</p>",
        "id": 614608640,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1785869646
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/ExistsUniqueAnd/near/614606912\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution_unique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">assumptions</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSolution</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution_also</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">assumptions</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MoreoverSatisfies</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">theSolution</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The disadvantage of this is that I would have to write (assumptions) twice.</p>",
        "id": 614608710,
        "sender_full_name": "Joris van Winden",
        "timestamp": 1785869672
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>variable</code>, and <code>include</code> if necessary</p>",
